      {
        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "fe2f3668-27a2-59de-ae82-dcfe2f14d039",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: H. P. Lovecraft, Timothy Leary, August Derleth, Donald Wandrei\n- Organizations: Arkham House\n- Places: Sauk City, Wisconsin\n- Works: Slan\n- Topics: horror fiction, psychedelic drugs, weird fiction, publishing\n\nFacts:\n- H. P. Lovecraft was born on August 20, 1890, and he was an American author who achieved posthumous fame through influential works of horror fiction.\n- Timothy Leary was born on October 22, 1920, and he was an American psychologist and writer known for advocating controlled exploration of the therapeutic potential of psychedelic drugs.\n- Arkham House was founded in 1939 in Sauk City, Wisconsin, by August Derleth and Donald Wandrei.\n- Arkham House specialized in weird fiction and was created to preserve the best fiction of H. P. Lovecraft in hardcover.\n- Slan was published in hardcover by Arkham House in 1946 in an edition of 4,051 copies.\n- H. P. Lovecraft died on March 15, 1937.\n- Timothy Leary died on May 31, 1996.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "308e273c-cd41-5526-a857-48c041f948c4",
        "text": "Page: H. P. Lovecraft. Sentence: Howard Phillips Lovecraft ( ; August 20, 1890 – March 15, 1937) was an American author who achieved posthumous fame through his influential works of horror fiction.\nPage: Timothy Leary. Sentence: Timothy Francis Leary (October 22, 1920 – May 31, 1996) was an American psychologist and writer known for advocating the exploration of the therapeutic potential of psychedelic drugs under controlled conditions.\nPage: Arkham House. Sentence: Arkham House is a publishing house specializing in weird fiction founded in Sauk City, Wisconsin in 1939 by August Derleth and Donald Wandrei to preserve in hardcover the best fiction of H. P. Lovecraft.\nPage: Slan. Sentence: It was subsequently published in hardcover in 1946 by Arkham House, in an edition of 4,051 copies.",
